  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The number of species having a square planar shape from the following is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>SF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>SiF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><msub><mi>BF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><msub><mi>BrF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Cu</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>PtCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridised with two lone pairs of electrons, hence, it is&nbsp;square planar.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math>&nbsp;hybridised with one&nbsp;lone pairs of electrons, hence, it is&nbsp;See saw.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SiF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> hybridised with zero&nbsp;lone pairs of electrons, hence, it is Tetrahedral</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><msub><mi>BF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> hybridised with zero lone pairs of electrons, hence, it is Tetrahedral</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi>Cu</mi><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>]</mo><msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo></math>is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>dsp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridised and is&nbsp;Square planar</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>]</mo><msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8211;</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridised and is Tetrahedral</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>PtCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>]</mo><msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8211;</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo></math>is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>dsp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridised and is&nbsp;Square planar</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><msub><mi>BrF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;with&nbsp;&nbsp;Square planar geometry.</p><p>So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> square planer shape compounds are present.</p></blockquote>"
  }
}